  "readmeFile": "ReadMe.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 7.0.451\n\nBreakingChange: TcAmsServerPInvoke.AmsConnectEx now takes an AmsServerReceiveDelegateEx; the previous signature crashed the native receive thread in 32-bit processes, #351635\n\nVersion 7.0.442\n\nEnh: AdsErrorCode.PortDisabled is classified as retryable (CanRetry), so RepeatedRead/RepeatedWrite retry while the TwinCAT router restarts, #349831\n\nVersion 7.0.410\n\nFix: TcAmsServerPInvoke.AmsConnect/AmsConnectEx registered a garbled AMS port name at the router, #337462\n\nEnh: Added AmsChannelSettings, holding the router loopback endpoint, channel port type, Unix domain socket path and router protocol of a single AdsClient/AdsServer instance. AmsConfiguration is now only the process wide preset for it, #338067\n\nEnh: SocketFactory and ChannelProtocolEvaluator got overloads taking an AmsChannelSettings. The existing overloads are unchanged and keep using the process wide AmsConfiguration defaults, #338067\n\nEnh: AmsNetId.IsSameTarget got an overload taking the local AmsNetId of the caller. It resolves the AmsNetId.LocalHost alias against the router that caller is attached to, instead of against the process wide AmsNetId.Local. Passing null keeps the previous behaviour, #338077\n\nVersion 7.0.403\n\nBreakingChange: IRouterNotificationProvider got a new RouterState property, #337368\n\nBreakingChange: The values of the AmsRouterState enumeration are realigned with the native AMSEVENT_ROUTER* constants (None = -1, Stopped = 0, Started = 1, Removed = 2), #337371\n\nVersion 7.0.382\n\nFix: ReadWithFallback/ReadWithFallbackAsync ignored the fallback index group, so reading the symbol upload info failed on older targets, #333682\n\nVersion 7.0.323\n\nFix: ADS server receive loop no longer spins at full CPU load when the opposite side closes the connection (e.g. TwinCAT System Service restart), #325658\n\nVersion 7.0.286\n\nFix: Several minor security issues in base classes used by TcpIPRouter fixed.\n\nVersion 7.0.280\n\nFix: Issue starting communication with 32-Bit TwinCAT (hanging on TcpLoopback)\n\nVersion 7.0.263\n\nBreakingChange: Removed the obsolete AdsErrorCode.Succeeded; use AdsErrorCode.NoError instead\n\nVersion 7.0.165\n\nEnh: IEnumValue.Value replaces IEnumValue.Primitive and IEnumValue.BaseType replaces IEnumValue.ManagedBaseType; the old properties are obsolete\n\nVersion 7.0.133\n\nEnh: New extension methods TwinCAT.Ads.AdsClientExtensions.RepeatedWriteAsync / TwinCAT.Ads.AdsClientExtensions.RepeatedWrite\n\nVersion 7.0.109\n\nEnh: Fewer memory allocations and copy operations for better performance\n\nVersion 7.0.36\n\nBreakingChange: Removed the net6.0 target (.NET 6 is out of support)\n\nVersion 7.0\n\nEnh: Supports locally installed TwinCAT 2 (via PInvoke channel)\n\nEnh: Supports internal communication via UnixSockets, TCP/IP Loopback and PInvoke\n\nEnh: TargetFramework dependencies changed to net8.0, net6.0, netstandard2.0",
